# Claude Code keeps its entire state under `$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, which `fish/config.fish` points at
# this directory. That means conversation transcripts (`projects/`), `history.jsonl`, `sessions/`,
# `shell-snapshots/`, and `.claude.json` all live inside a public git repository.
#
# The root `.gitignore` already excludes everything with `/*`, so nothing here is tracked by
# accident today. This file is a second layer: if the root pattern is ever narrowed, the default
# here stays "ignore everything" and only the two files below become trackable.
#
# Neither layer survives `git add -f .`, which bypasses all ignore rules. Force-add individual
# paths, never a directory.

*
!.gitignore
!settings.json
